[
  {
    "sha": "455a2c2fc8f01148a018e9288584f440eab667fc",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV1WsOtoAKDQ1NWEyYzJmYzhmMDExNDhhMDE4ZTkyODg1ODRmNDQwZWFiNjY3ZmM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T15:41:51Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-26T15:41:51Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(pocket3d): start and exit picks for 3D Pocket\n\nThe 3D Pocket takes a start point and an exit point (Region pick).\nEach level's first ring starts at its point nearest the start point,\nlaps back to it and runs on to its old start, so every link stays the\nautomatic one; zigzag rows start at their nearer end. The last ring\nruns on to its point nearest the exit point. The descent goes through\nthe ladder's entry rule. A start, a descent or an exit beyond reach, an\nAdaptive (HSM) level, Adaptive or Rest roughing in the app, and a moved\ncolumn within the tool radius of the part (exact clip and\nsegment-to-facet check) are refused by name. No pick is the old path,\nbyte for byte.\n\nRefs #3329\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "edb96f14b24dd08945cd93a0ad1fdcf2b3bbdcc4",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/git/trees/edb96f14b24dd08945cd93a0ad1fdcf2b3bbdcc4"
